module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Koszul.Sheaf.CoordinateContractionDegreeOne
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulContractionClass
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulHomComplexVanishing
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Cohomology.InternalHom.EvaluatingSectionsSums
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Cohomology.StrictlyPerfect.BoundedAboveHomComparison
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Sheafification.LocalRepresentatives

/-!
# The first self-Ext sheaf of a Koszul-regular quotient is generated by the contractions

Let `(X, O♯)` be a ringed space, let `φ : (O♯)ʳ ⟶ O♯` be a morphism of sheaves of modules whose
Koszul complex `K` resolves the quotient `O♯/I`, and read `K` as a cochain complex. The first
cohomology sheaf of the internal endomorphism complex `SheafHom^•(K, K)` is the first self-Ext
sheaf of the quotient, and the coordinate contractions `δ₁, …, δ_r` give `r` global sections
`[δⱼ]` of it (`Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.contractionClass`). This file proves that
those sections **generate** it: every local section of `H¹(SheafHom(K, K))` is, on a covering of
its domain, an `O♯`-linear combination of the `[δⱼ]`.

That is the local structure of degree-one self-Ext classes, and it is what makes the
Koszul relations among the `δⱼ` say anything about an arbitrary class. It is not formal: a
degree-one cocycle of `SheafHom^•(K, K)` is an arbitrary family of degree-lowering morphisms
anticommuting with the differential, and nothing about such a family forces it to be a
combination of contractions on the nose. What is true is that it becomes one after passing to
cohomology and restricting to a covering, and the argument has three steps.

**One.** The augmentation `K ⟶ O♯/I` is a quasi-isomorphism and `K` is bounded above with terms
direct summands of finite free modules, so the induced morphism of internal Hom complexes

`SheafHom^•(K, K) ⟶ SheafHom^•(K, O♯/I)`

is a quasi-isomorphism (Stacks 08I5). In particular it is an isomorphism on `H¹`, so two
degree-one cocycles of `SheafHom^•(K, K)` are cohomologous on an open set as soon as their
composites with the augmentation agree there.

**Two.** The target `O♯/I` is concentrated in degree zero, so a degree-one section of
`SheafHom^•(K, O♯/I)` has one nonvanishing component, the one out of the degree-one term of `K`;
and that term is the free sheaf `(O♯)ʳ`, whose sections over any object are *exactly* the
`O♯`-linear combinations of the `r` tautological ones. So the composite with the augmentation is
determined by its `r` values on those sections.

**Three.** Those `r` values are sections of `O♯/I`, and the quotient map `O♯ ⟶ O♯/I` is an
epimorphism, hence locally surjective: on a covering of the domain each of them lifts to a
section `aⱼ` of `O♯`. The combination `Σⱼ aⱼ δⱼ` then has the same composite with the
augmentation as the given cocycle, because `δⱼ` sends the `k`-th tautological section of
`(O♯)ʳ` to the Kronecker delta
(`Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.chainXZeroIsoUnit_coordKoszulD_chainXOneIso_inv`), so by
step one the two are cohomologous there.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.augSingle`: the augmentation of the Koszul cochain
  complex into the complex concentrated in degree zero on the quotient.
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.homAug`: the induced morphism
  `SheafHom^•(K, K) ⟶ SheafHom^•(K, O♯/I)`.
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.quotientPi`: the quotient map `O♯ ⟶ O♯/I`, read into
  the degree-zero term of the single complex.
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.extGenerator`: **the morphism from `(O♯)ʳ` to the
  first cohomology sheaf of `SheafHom^•(K, K)` carrying the `j`-th tautological section to the
  class of `δⱼ`.**
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.cochainOneBasis` and `cochainOneCoord`: the
  tautological sections of the degree `-1` term of the Koszul cochain complex and the
  coordinates of a local section with respect to them.
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.contractionCombinationCycle`: the cocycle
  `Σⱼ aⱼ δⱼ` attached to a family of local sections of `O♯`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.quasiIso_homAug`: **step one**, the morphism of
  internal Hom complexes induced by the augmentation is a quasi-isomorphism.
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.homAug_f_one_ext`: **step two**, two degree-one
  sections of `SheafHom^•(K, K)` have the same image in `SheafHom^•(K, O♯/I)` as soon as their
  composites with the augmentation agree on every local section of the degree `-1` term.
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.homologyπ_eq_of_homAug`: two degree-one cocycles with
  the same image in `SheafHom^•(K, O♯/I)` are cohomologous.
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.augSingle_f_zero_coordKoszulD`: the composite of `δⱼ`
  with the augmentation reads off the `j`-th coordinate.
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.imageSieve_extGenerator_homologyπ_mem` and
  `isLocallySurjective_extGenerator`: **the conclusion** — the class of a degree-one cocycle
  is locally in the image of `extGenerator`, so `extGenerator` is locally surjective.

## Implementation notes

**Why the comparison is with the Hom complex into the quotient and not with an Ext sheaf.** The
first Ext sheaf of the quotient is identified with `SheafHom(⋀¹((O♯)ʳ), O♯/I)` in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulExtComputation`, through the vanishing of
the differential of the Hom complex into the quotient. That identification is not used here:
what the argument needs is not the value of the Ext sheaf but the *injectivity on sections* of
the comparison with the Hom complex into the quotient, and that is exactly the quasi-isomorphy
of step one together with the monomorphy of the inclusion of cycles. Comparing cocycles directly
avoids both the degreewise product description of a term of the Hom complex and the transport
through the two readings of a complex concentrated in degree zero.

**The two spellings of the structure sheaf.** Sheaves of modules on the space are indexed by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.structureSheaf`, while the free sheaf `(O♯)ʳ` carrying the Koszul data is
indexed by `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat`; the two name the same sheaf of rings but only after
unfolding `sheafCompose`, so instance search does not identify them. Accordingly
`koszulCoord` and `ofCochainOne` are definitions whose only content is to read a coordinate, or
a local section of the degree `-1` term, at the spelling in which the module structure its
consumer needs is found.

**The ringed-site API is stated at a third spelling of the same sheaf of rings.** The internal
Hom complex of a ringed site is stated over the canonical
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O`, while the complexes here live in
`StructureSheafModules Rc`, whose ring sheaf goes through `CategoryTheory.sheafCompose`. The two
are the same sheaf of rings by `rfl`, but each goes through a plain definition, so a goal written
in one does not match a lemma written in the other at the transparency a rewrite uses; both are
made `implicit_reducible` for the file, as in
`StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Cohomology.InternalHom.ExtFromStrictlyPerfectResolution`. That
transparency is not available to instance search, which cannot be raised to it in the same file,
so `quasiIso_homAug` hands `quasiIso_augSingle` to Stacks 08I5 positionally rather than leaving
it to be synthesised.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BQY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BQY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08I5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08I5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 062L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/062L)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Sheaf Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry HomologicalComplex CochainComplex.HomComplex
open Stacks.ChainComplex Stacks.SheafOfModules

universe u

attribute [local implicit_reducible] CategoryTheory.sheafCompose
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf

namespace Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable {X : TopCat.{u}} (Rc : TopCat.Sheaf CommRingCat.{u} X)
  [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [(Opens.grothendieckTopology X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  {r : ℕ}
  {A : SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X)
    (koszulFreeSheaf Rc r)}
  {φ : koszulFreeSheaf Rc r ⟶
    SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)}
  (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ)

/-- The quotient, as a cochain complex concentrated in degree zero. -/
noncomputable abbrev quotientSingle : CochainComplex (StructureSheafModules Rc) ℤ :=
  (single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj (quotient Rc (φ := φ))

/-- The augmentation into the cochain complex concentrated in degree zero. -/
noncomputable def augSingle : cochain Rc K ⟶ quotientSingle Rc (φ := φ) :=
  cochainAugmentation Rc K ≫ (quotientSingleIso Rc (φ := φ)).hom

/-- **The augmentation into the cochain complex concentrated in degree zero is a
quasi-isomorphism** as soon as the augmentation of the Koszul chain complex is: the two readings
of the complex concentrated in degree zero are isomorphic. -/
instance quasiIso_augSingle [QuasiIso K.augmentation] : QuasiIso (augSingle Rc K) := by
  rw [augSingle]
  infer_instance

/-- **The morphism of internal Hom complexes induced by the augmentation**, from the
endomorphism complex of the Koszul cochain complex to the Hom complex into the quotient. -/
noncomputable def homAug :
    endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K) ⟶
      (RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        (quotientSingle Rc (φ := φ))).obj :=
  RingedSite.homMap (ringedSite Rc) (𝟙 (cochain Rc K)) (augSingle Rc K)

/-- **The Koszul cochain complex vanishes below `-r`**, because the Koszul chain complex
vanishes above the rank. -/
theorem isZero_cochain_X_of_lt_neg (i : ℤ) (hi : i < -(r : ℤ)) :
    IsZero ((cochain Rc K).X i) :=
  (Stacks.ChainComplex.isZero_asCochain_X_iff K.chain i).2
    (IsZero.of_iso (RingedSite.isZero_exteriorPiece_of_card_lt (ringedSite Rc) A
        (ULift.{u} (Fin r)) (Iso.refl _) (-i) (by simpa using (by omega : (r : ℤ) < -i)))
      (eqToIso (K.chain_X (-i))))

/-- **The morphism of internal Hom complexes induced by the augmentation is a
quasi-isomorphism.** The source complex of the Hom complexes is bounded above with terms direct
summands of finite free modules, and both targets vanish below `-r`, so this is the
quasi-isomorphism invariance of the internal Hom complex (Stacks 08I5) applied to the
augmentation.

This is what makes a comparison of degree-one cocycles possible: the induced map on the first
cohomology sheaves is an isomorphism, hence injective on local sections. -/
instance quasiIso_homAug [QuasiIso K.augmentation] : QuasiIso (homAug Rc K) :=
  @RingedSite.homMap_quasiIso_of_boundedAbove_isFiniteFreeSummand (ringedSite Rc)
    (cochain Rc K) (cochain Rc K) (quotientSingle Rc (φ := φ)) (-(r : ℤ))
    (isZero_cochain_X_of_lt_neg Rc K)
    (fun i hi => isZero_single_obj_X _ 0 _ i (by omega))
    ⟨0, fun i hi => (Stacks.ChainComplex.isZero_asCochain_X_iff K.chain i).2
      (K.isZero_chain_X_of_neg (by omega))⟩
    (isFiniteFreeSummand_cochain_X Rc K) (augSingle Rc K) (quasiIso_augSingle Rc K)

/-- **Two degree-one sections of `SheafHom^•(K, K)` have the same image in
`SheafHom^•(K, O♯/I)` as soon as their composites with the augmentation agree on every local
section of the degree `-1` term.** The target is concentrated in degree zero, so every other
component of the image lands in a zero object and nothing is to be checked there. -/
theorem homAug_f_one_ext (W : Opens ↥X)
    (f g : ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).X 1).val.obj (op W))
    (h : ∀ (W' : Opens ↥X) (i : W' ⟶ W) (x : ((cochain Rc K).X (-1)).val.obj (op W')),
      ((augSingle Rc K).f 0).val.app (op W')
          (RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver (ringedSite Rc) (endHom Rc K) W W' i 1 (-1) 0
            (by omega) f x) =
        ((augSingle Rc K).f 0).val.app (op W')
          (RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver (ringedSite Rc) (endHom Rc K) W W' i 1 (-1) 0
            (by omega) g x)) :
    ((homAug Rc K).f 1).val.app (op W) f = ((homAug Rc K).f 1).val.app (op W) g := by
  refine RingedSite.homSection_ext (ringedSite Rc)
    (RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K) (quotientSingle Rc (φ := φ)))
    W 1 ?_
  intro p q hpq W' i x
  rw [homAug, RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver_homMap, RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver_homMap]
  rcases eq_or_ne q 0 with rfl | hq
  · obtain rfl : p = -1 := by omega
    exact h W' i x
  · refine Eq.trans (Stacks.SheafOfModules.section_eq_zero_of_isZero ?_ (op W') _)
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.section_eq_zero_of_isZero ?_ (op W') _).symm
    · exact isZero_single_obj_X _ 0 _ q hq
    · exact isZero_single_obj_X _ 0 _ q hq

/-- **The degree-zero component of the augmentation is an epimorphism.** It is the quotient map
`O♯ ⟶ O♯/I` composed with the identifications of the degree-zero terms of the two complexes with
`O♯` and with `O♯/I`. -/
instance epi_augSingle_f_zero : Epi ((augSingle Rc K).f 0) := by
  have h1 : Epi K.chainXZeroIsoUnit.hom := inferInstance
  have h2 : Epi (koszulQuotientπ φ) := inferInstance
  have h3 : Epi (HomologicalComplex.singleObjXSelf (ComplexShape.down ℤ) 0
      (koszulQuotient.{u, u, u} φ)).inv := inferInstance
  have h4 : Epi (((quotientSingleIso Rc (φ := φ)).hom).f 0) := inferInstance
  have haz : K.augmentationZero = K.chainXZeroIsoUnit.hom ≫ koszulQuotientπ φ := rfl
  have h : (augSingle Rc K).f 0 = K.chainXZeroIsoUnit.hom ≫ koszulQuotientπ φ ≫
      ((HomologicalComplex.singleObjXSelf (ComplexShape.down ℤ) 0
          (koszulQuotient.{u, u, u} φ)).inv ≫ ((quotientSingleIso Rc (φ := φ)).hom).f 0) := by
    rw [show (augSingle Rc K).f 0 = K.augmentation.f 0 ≫
        ((quotientSingleIso Rc (φ := φ)).hom).f 0 from rfl,
      K.augmentation_f_zero, haz]
    exact Category.assoc _ _ _
  rw [h]
  exact epi_comp' h1 (epi_comp' h2 (epi_comp' h3 h4))

/-- The quotient map, read into the degree-zero term of the single complex. -/
noncomputable def quotientPi :
    SheafOfModules.unit (structureSheaf Rc) ⟶ (quotientSingle Rc (φ := φ)).X 0 :=
  K.chainXZeroIsoUnit.inv ≫ (augSingle Rc K).f 0

/-- **The quotient map, read into the degree-zero term of the single complex, is an
epimorphism.** -/
instance epi_quotientPi : Epi (quotientPi Rc K) := by
  have h1 : Epi K.chainXZeroIsoUnit.inv := inferInstance
  have h2 : Epi ((augSingle Rc K).f 0) := inferInstance
  rw [quotientPi]
  exact epi_comp' h1 h2

/-- The degree-zero component of the augmentation is the identification of the degree-zero term
of the Koszul complex with `O♯` followed by the quotient map. -/
theorem chainXZeroIsoUnit_comp_quotientPi :
    K.chainXZeroIsoUnit.hom ≫ quotientPi Rc K = (augSingle Rc K).f 0 :=
  Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc _ _

/-- **The quotient map is locally surjective:** every local section of `O♯/I` is, on a covering
of its domain, the image of a section of `O♯`. This is the one place where the argument has to
shrink the open set. -/
instance isLocallySurjective_quotientPi :
    PresheafOfModules.IsLocallySurjective (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X)
      (quotientPi Rc K).val :=
  ImageSubsheaf.isLocallySurjective_of_epi _

/-- The degree-one generator of the self-Ext algebra. -/
noncomputable def extGenerator :
    koszulFreeSheaf Rc r ⟶ (endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).homology 1 :=
  ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).homology 1).freeHomEquiv.symm (contractionClass Rc K)

/-- The degree-one generator carries the `j`-th tautological section of `(O♯)ʳ` to the
cohomology class of `δⱼ`. -/
theorem extGenerator_val_app_freeSection (U : (Opens ↥X)ᵒᵖ) (k : ULift.{u} (Fin r)) :
    (extGenerator Rc K).val.app U
        ((SheafOfModules.freeSection
          (R := toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc) k).val U) =
      contractionClassOn Rc K k U :=
  congrArg (fun t : ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).homology 1).sections => t.val U)
    (congrFun (((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).homology 1).freeHomEquiv.apply_symm_apply
      (contractionClass Rc K)) k)

/-- The `l`-th coordinate of a local section of the free sheaf of modules. -/
noncomputable def koszulCoord (V : (Opens ↥X)ᵒᵖ) (e : (koszulFreeSheaf Rc r).val.obj V)
    (l : ULift.{u} (Fin r)) : (structureSheaf Rc).obj.obj V :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeCoord (S := toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc) V e l

/-- The `j`-th coordinate functional of the free sheaf of modules reads off the `j`-th
coordinate. -/
theorem coordExteriorFunctional_dual_eq_koszulCoord (j : ULift.{u} (Fin r))
    (V : (Opens ↥X)ᵒᵖ) (m : (koszulFreeSheaf Rc r).val.obj V) :
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.coordExteriorFunctional
        (Osharp := Rc) (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) j).dual V m =
      koszulCoord Rc V m j := by
  refine Eq.trans (Stacks.SheafOfModules.coordExteriorFunctional_dual_apply j V m) ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (congrFun (Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeCoordLinearEquiv_apply
    (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc).property V m) j)
  simp [Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeCoordBasis, Module.Basis.map_repr]

/-- **The degree-one generator on a local section of `(O♯)ʳ`:** it is the combination of the
classes of the contractions with the coordinates of the section as coefficients. -/
theorem extGenerator_val_app (V : (Opens ↥X)ᵒᵖ) (e : (koszulFreeSheaf Rc r).val.obj V) :
    (extGenerator Rc K).val.app V e =
      ∑ l, koszulCoord Rc V e l • contractionClassOn Rc K l V := by
  have h := Stacks.SheafOfModules.app_eq_sum_smul_freeCoord (extGenerator Rc K) V e
  have h2 : ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).homology 1).freeHomEquiv (extGenerator Rc K)
      = contractionClass Rc K :=
    ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).homology 1).freeHomEquiv.apply_symm_apply _
  refine h.trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun l _ => ?_)
  exact congrArg
    (fun t : ULift.{u} (Fin r) → ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).homology 1).sections =>
      koszulCoord Rc V e l • PresheafOfModules.sections.eval (t l) V) h2

/-- A local section of the degree `-1` term of the Koszul cochain complex, read as a section of
the degree-one term of the Koszul chain complex. -/
noncomputable def ofCochainOne (V : (Opens ↥X)ᵒᵖ)
    (x : ((cochain Rc K).X (-1)).val.obj V) : (K.chain.X 1).val.obj V := x

/-- The `l`-th basis section of the degree `-1` term of the Koszul cochain complex. -/
noncomputable def cochainOneBasis (l : ULift.{u} (Fin r)) (V : (Opens ↥X)ᵒᵖ) :
    ((cochain Rc K).X (-1)).val.obj V :=
  K.chainXOneIso.inv.val.app V
    (PresheafOfModules.sections.eval (SheafOfModules.freeSection
      (R := toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc) l) V)

/-- The `l`-th coordinate of a local section of the degree `-1` term. -/
noncomputable def cochainOneCoord (V : (Opens ↥X)ᵒᵖ)
    (x : ((cochain Rc K).X (-1)).val.obj V) (l : ULift.{u} (Fin r)) :
    (structureSheaf Rc).obj.obj V :=
  koszulCoord Rc V
    (K.chainXOneIso.hom.val.app V (ofCochainOne Rc K V x)) l

/-- The tautological sections of the degree `-1` term are compatible with restriction. -/
theorem cochainOneBasis_map {V W : (Opens ↥X)ᵒᵖ} (f : V ⟶ W) (l : ULift.{u} (Fin r)) :
    ((cochain Rc K).X (-1)).val.map f (cochainOneBasis Rc K l V) = cochainOneBasis Rc K l W :=
  (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply K.chainXOneIso.inv.val f _).symm.trans
    (congrArg (fun z => K.chainXOneIso.inv.val.app W z)
      (PresheafOfModules.sections_property _ f))

/-- **Every local section of the degree `-1` term of the Koszul cochain complex is the
combination of the tautological sections with its own coordinates as coefficients.** The term is
the free sheaf `(O♯)ʳ` read through the identification of the degree-one term of the Koszul chain
complex, and the sections of a finite free sheaf of modules over an object are freely spanned by
the tautological ones -- with no shrinking of the open set. -/
theorem eq_sum_smul_cochainOneBasis (V : (Opens ↥X)ᵒᵖ)
    (x : ((cochain Rc K).X (-1)).val.obj V) :
    ∑ l, cochainOneCoord Rc K V x l • cochainOneBasis Rc K l V = x := by
  have h := Stacks.SheafOfModules.app_eq_sum_smul_freeCoord
    (𝟙 (koszulFreeSheaf Rc r)) V
    (K.chainXOneIso.hom.val.app V (ofCochainOne Rc K V x))
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (SheafOfModules.iso_inv_hom_app_apply K.chainXOneIso V
    (ofCochainOne Rc K V x))
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (congrArg (fun z => K.chainXOneIso.inv.val.app V z) h.symm)
  rw [map_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun l _ => ?_
  exact (map_smul (ConcreteCategory.hom (K.chainXOneIso.inv.val.app V))
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeCoord
      (S := toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc) V
      (K.chainXOneIso.hom.val.app V (ofCochainOne Rc K V x)) l)
    (PresheafOfModules.sections.eval (SheafOfModules.freeSection
      (R := toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc) l) V)).symm

/-- **The composite of `δⱼ` with the augmentation reads off the `j`-th coordinate**, through the
quotient map. This is where the Koszul-specific input enters: `δⱼ` is the `j`-th coordinate
projection in the lowest degree. -/
theorem augSingle_f_zero_coordKoszulD (l : ULift.{u} (Fin r)) (V : (Opens ↥X)ᵒᵖ)
    (x : ((cochain Rc K).X (-1)).val.obj V) :
    ((augSingle Rc K).f 0).val.app V
        ((K.coordKoszulD l (show (0 : ℤ) + 1 = 1 by norm_num)).val.app V
          (ofCochainOne Rc K V x)) =
      (quotientPi Rc K).val.app V (cochainOneCoord Rc K V x l) := by
  refine Eq.trans (SheafOfModules.hom_congr_app_apply
    (chainXZeroIsoUnit_comp_quotientPi Rc K).symm V _) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (SheafOfModules.comp_val_app_apply _ _ V _) ?_
  refine congrArg (fun z => (quotientPi Rc K).val.app V z) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun z => K.chainXZeroIsoUnit.hom.val.app V
      ((K.coordKoszulD l (show (0 : ℤ) + 1 = 1 by norm_num)).val.app V z))
    (SheafOfModules.iso_inv_hom_app_apply K.chainXOneIso V
      (ofCochainOne Rc K V x)).symm) ?_
  exact (K.chainXZeroIsoUnit_coordKoszulD_chainXOneIso_inv l V _).trans
    (coordExteriorFunctional_dual_eq_koszulCoord Rc l V _)

/-- Commuting squares of morphisms of sheaves of modules commute on local sections. -/
private theorem app_comp_eq_app_comp {C : Type*} [Category C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
    {R : Sheaf J RingCat} {M N P Q : SheafOfModules R} (a : M ⟶ N) (b : N ⟶ Q) (c : M ⟶ P)
    (d : P ⟶ Q) (h : a ≫ b = c ≫ d) (V : Cᵒᵖ) (x : M.val.obj V) :
    b.val.app V (a.val.app V x) = d.val.app V (c.val.app V x) :=
  SheafOfModules.hom_congr_app_apply h V x

/-- **Two degree-one cocycles with the same image in `SheafHom^•(K, O♯/I)` are cohomologous.**
The induced map on the first cohomology sheaves is an isomorphism, hence injective on local
sections, and the inclusion of cycles is a monomorphism. -/
theorem homologyπ_eq_of_homAug [QuasiIso K.augmentation] (W : Opens ↥X)
    (y z : ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).cycles 1).val.obj (op W))
    (h : ((homAug Rc K).f 1).val.app (op W)
          (((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).iCycles 1).val.app (op W) y) =
        ((homAug Rc K).f 1).val.app (op W)
          (((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).iCycles 1).val.app (op W) z)) :
    ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).homologyπ 1).val.app (op W) y =
      ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).homologyπ 1).val.app (op W) z := by
  have hiso : IsIso (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap (homAug Rc K) 1) :=
    (quasiIsoAt_iff_isIso_homologyMap (homAug Rc K) 1).1 inferInstance
  have hcy : (HomologicalComplex.cyclesMap (homAug Rc K) 1).val.app (op W) y
      = (HomologicalComplex.cyclesMap (homAug Rc K) 1).val.app (op W) z := by
    refine injective_app_of_mono
      ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        (quotientSingle Rc (φ := φ))).obj.iCycles 1) (op W) ?_
    rw [app_comp_eq_app_comp _ _ _ _ (HomologicalComplex.cyclesMap_i (homAug Rc K) 1),
      app_comp_eq_app_comp _ _ _ _ (HomologicalComplex.cyclesMap_i (homAug Rc K) 1)]
    exact h
  refine injective_app_of_mono (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap (homAug Rc K) 1) (op W) ?_
  rw [app_comp_eq_app_comp _ _ _ _ (HomologicalComplex.homologyπ_naturality (homAug Rc K) 1),
    app_comp_eq_app_comp _ _ _ _ (HomologicalComplex.homologyπ_naturality (homAug Rc K) 1), hcy]

/-- Evaluating the contraction section in the degrees `(-1, 0)` of the cochain complex returns
the contraction from exterior degree one to exterior degree zero. -/
theorem applyHomSectionOver_contractionSection_degreeOne (l : ULift.{u} (Fin r))
    (U V : Opens ↥X) (i : V ⟶ U) (x : ((cochain Rc K).X (-1)).val.obj (op V)) :
    RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver (ringedSite Rc) (endHom Rc K) U V i 1 (-1) 0 (by omega)
        (contractionSection Rc K l U) x =
      (K.coordKoszulD l (show (0 : ℤ) + 1 = 1 by norm_num)).val.app (op V)
        (ofCochainOne Rc K (op V) x) :=
  applyHomSectionOver_contractionSection Rc K l U V i (-1) 0 (by omega) x

/-- **The cocycle `Σⱼ aⱼ δⱼ` attached to a family of local sections `aⱼ` of `O♯`.** -/
noncomputable def contractionCombinationCycle (W : Opens ↥X)
    (a : ULift.{u} (Fin r) → (structureSheaf Rc).obj.obj (op W)) :
    ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).cycles 1).val.obj (op W) :=
  ∑ l, a l • (contractionCycle Rc K l).val.app (op W)
    (1 : (structureSheaf Rc).obj.obj (op W))

/-- The combination cocycle is, inside the complex, the combination of the contraction
sections. -/
theorem iCycles_contractionCombinationCycle (W : Opens ↥X)
    (a : ULift.{u} (Fin r) → (structureSheaf Rc).obj.obj (op W)) :
    ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).iCycles 1).val.app (op W)
        (contractionCombinationCycle Rc K W a) =
      ∑ l, a l • contractionSection Rc K l W := by
  rw [contractionCombinationCycle, map_sum]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun l _ =>
    (map_smul _ _ _).trans (congrArg (fun z => a l • z) (iCycles_contractionCycle Rc K l (op W)))

/-- The class of the combination cocycle is the combination of the classes of the
contractions. -/
theorem homologyπ_contractionCombinationCycle (W : Opens ↥X)
    (a : ULift.{u} (Fin r) → (structureSheaf Rc).obj.obj (op W)) :
    ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).homologyπ 1).val.app (op W)
        (contractionCombinationCycle Rc K W a) =
      ∑ l, a l • contractionClassOn Rc K l (op W) := by
  rw [contractionCombinationCycle, map_sum]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun l _ => map_smul _ _ _

/-- **Evaluating the combination `Σⱼ aⱼ δⱼ` and composing with the augmentation** gives the
combination of the coordinates of the argument with the restrictions of the `aⱼ` as
coefficients. -/
theorem eval_contractionCombination (W : Opens ↥X)
    (a : ULift.{u} (Fin r) → (structureSheaf Rc).obj.obj (op W))
    (W' : Opens ↥X) (i : W' ⟶ W) (x : ((cochain Rc K).X (-1)).val.obj (op W')) :
    ((augSingle Rc K).f 0).val.app (op W')
        (RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver (ringedSite Rc) (endHom Rc K) W W' i 1 (-1) 0 (by omega)
          (∑ l, a l • contractionSection Rc K l W) x) =
      ∑ l, (structureSheaf Rc).obj.map i.op (a l) •
        (quotientPi Rc K).val.app (op W') (cochainOneCoord Rc K (op W') x l) := by
  rw [RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver_sum_left, map_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun l _ => ?_
  rw [RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver_smul_left, map_smul,
    applyHomSectionOver_contractionSection_degreeOne, augSingle_f_zero_coordKoszulD]
  rfl

/-- **Evaluating any degree-one section of `SheafHom^•(K, K)` and composing with the
augmentation** is determined by the `r` values on the tautological sections, the coordinates of
the argument being the coefficients. -/
theorem eval_section_eq_sum (W : Opens ↥X)
    (s : ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).X 1).val.obj (op W))
    (W' : Opens ↥X) (i : W' ⟶ W) (x : ((cochain Rc K).X (-1)).val.obj (op W')) :
    ((augSingle Rc K).f 0).val.app (op W')
        (RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver (ringedSite Rc) (endHom Rc K) W W' i 1 (-1) 0 (by omega)
          s x) =
      ∑ l, cochainOneCoord Rc K (op W') x l •
        ((augSingle Rc K).f 0).val.app (op W')
          (RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver (ringedSite Rc) (endHom Rc K) W W' i 1 (-1) 0
            (by omega) s (cochainOneBasis Rc K l (op W'))) := by
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun z => ((augSingle Rc K).f 0).val.app (op W')
    (RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver (ringedSite Rc) (endHom Rc K) W W' i 1 (-1) 0 (by omega)
      s z)) (eq_sum_smul_cochainOneBasis Rc K (op W') x).symm) ?_
  rw [RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver_sum_right, map_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun l _ => ?_
  rw [RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver_smul_right, map_smul]

/-- The `l`-th value of the augmented cocycle on the basis sections. -/
noncomputable def cocycleAugValue (V : Opens ↥X)
    (c : ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).cycles 1).val.obj (op V))
    (l : ULift.{u} (Fin r)) : ((quotientSingle Rc (φ := φ)).X 0).val.obj (op V) :=
  ((augSingle Rc K).f 0).val.app (op V)
    (RingedSite.applyHomSection (ringedSite Rc) (endHom Rc K) V 1 (-1) 0 (by omega)
      (((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).iCycles 1).val.app (op V) c)
      (cochainOneBasis Rc K l (op V)))

/-- **The values of a restricted cocycle on the tautological sections are the restrictions of its
values.** Both the evaluation and the augmentation commute with restriction, and the tautological
sections are themselves compatible with restriction. -/
theorem eval_restrict_cochainOneBasis (V : Opens ↥X)
    (c : ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).cycles 1).val.obj (op V))
    (W : Opens ↥X) (g : W ⟶ V) (W' : Opens ↥X) (i : W' ⟶ W) (l : ULift.{u} (Fin r)) :
    ((augSingle Rc K).f 0).val.app (op W')
        (RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver (ringedSite Rc) (endHom Rc K) W W' i 1 (-1) 0 (by omega)
          (((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).X 1).val.map g.op
            (((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).iCycles 1).val.app (op V) c))
          (cochainOneBasis Rc K l (op W'))) =
      ((quotientSingle Rc (φ := φ)).X 0).val.map i.op
        (((quotientSingle Rc (φ := φ)).X 0).val.map g.op (cocycleAugValue Rc K V c l)) := by
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun z => ((augSingle Rc K).f 0).val.app (op W') z)
    (RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver_restrict_comp (ringedSite Rc) (endHom Rc K) V W W' g i
      1 (-1) 0 (by omega)
      (((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).iCycles 1).val.app (op V) c)
      (cochainOneBasis Rc K l (op W'))).symm) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun z => ((augSingle Rc K).f 0).val.app (op W')
    (RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver (ringedSite Rc) (endHom Rc K) V W' (i ≫ g) 1 (-1) 0
      (by omega) (((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).iCycles 1).val.app (op V) c) z))
    (cochainOneBasis_map Rc K (i ≫ g).op l).symm) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun z => ((augSingle Rc K).f 0).val.app (op W') z)
    (RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver_map (ringedSite Rc) (endHom Rc K) V W' (i ≫ g) 1 (-1) 0
      (by omega) (((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).iCycles 1).val.app (op V) c)
      (cochainOneBasis Rc K l (op V)))) ?_
  exact (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply ((augSingle Rc K).f 0).val (i ≫ g).op _).trans
    (((quotientSingle Rc (φ := φ)).X 0).val.map_comp_apply g.op i.op _)

attribute [local instance] RingedSite.ringSheafSectionsCommRing

/-- **The class of a degree-one cocycle is, on a covering of its domain, an `O♯`-linear
combination of the classes of the coordinate contractions.**

The `r` values of the cocycle on the tautological sections, composed with the augmentation, are
sections of `O♯/I`; the quotient map is locally surjective, so on the intersection of the `r`
resulting coverings they lift to sections `aⱼ` of `O♯`. The cocycle `Σⱼ aⱼ δⱼ` then has the same
composite with the augmentation as the given one -- both are determined by their `r` values on
the tautological sections, and there they agree by the choice of the `aⱼ` and the fact that `δⱼ`
is the `j`-th coordinate -- so the two are cohomologous. -/
theorem imageSieve_extGenerator_homologyπ_mem [QuasiIso K.augmentation] (V : Opens ↥X)
    (c : ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).cycles 1).val.obj (op V)) :
    Presheaf.imageSieve ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (structureSheaf Rc).obj).map
        (extGenerator Rc K).val)
        (((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).homologyπ 1).val.app (op V) c) ∈
      Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X V := by
  classical
  refine (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X).superset_covering ?_
    (Stacks.Sheafification.finsetInf_covering (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Finset.univ
      (fun l : ULift.{u} (Fin r) => Presheaf.imageSieve
        ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (structureSheaf Rc).obj).map (quotientPi Rc K).val)
        (cocycleAugValue Rc K V c l))
      (fun l => Presheaf.imageSieve_mem (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) _ _))
  intro W g hg
  choose a ha using fun l : ULift.{u} (Fin r) =>
    Finset.inf_le (f := fun l : ULift.{u} (Fin r) => Presheaf.imageSieve
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (structureSheaf Rc).obj).map (quotientPi Rc K).val)
      (cocycleAugValue Rc K V c l)) (Finset.mem_univ l) g hg
  have ha' : ∀ l, (quotientPi Rc K).val.app (op W) (a l)
      = ((quotientSingle Rc (φ := φ)).X 0).val.map g.op (cocycleAugValue Rc K V c l) := ha
  refine ⟨Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeMk (op W) a, ?_⟩
  refine Eq.trans (extGenerator_val_app Rc K (op W)
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeMk (op W) a)) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun l _ =>
    congrArg (fun z => z • contractionClassOn Rc K l (op W))
      (congrFun (Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeCoord_freeMk (op W) a) l)) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (homologyπ_contractionCombinationCycle Rc K W a).symm ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply
    ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).homologyπ 1).val g.op c)
  refine homologyπ_eq_of_homAug Rc K W _ _ ?_
  refine homAug_f_one_ext Rc K W _ _ ?_
  intro W' i x
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun z => ((augSingle Rc K).f 0).val.app (op W')
      (RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver (ringedSite Rc) (endHom Rc K) W W' i 1 (-1) 0
        (by omega) z x))
    (iCycles_contractionCombinationCycle Rc K W a)) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (eval_contractionCombination Rc K W a W' i x) ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (congrArg (fun z => ((augSingle Rc K).f 0).val.app (op W')
      (RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver (ringedSite Rc) (endHom Rc K) W W' i 1 (-1) 0
        (by omega) z x))
    (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply
      ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).iCycles 1).val g.op c).symm)
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (eval_section_eq_sum Rc K W
    (((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).X 1).val.map g.op
      (((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).iCycles 1).val.app (op V) c)) W' i x).symm
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun l _ => ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (congrArg (fun z => cochainOneCoord Rc K (op W') x l • z)
    (eval_restrict_cochainOneBasis Rc K V c W g W' i l)).symm
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (congrArg (fun z => cochainOneCoord Rc K (op W') x l •
      ((quotientSingle Rc (φ := φ)).X 0).val.map i.op z) (ha' l))
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (congrArg (fun z => cochainOneCoord Rc K (op W') x l • z)
    (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (quotientPi Rc K).val i.op (a l)))
  refine Eq.trans ((map_smul (ConcreteCategory.hom ((quotientPi Rc K).val.app (op W')))
      ((structureSheaf Rc).obj.map i.op (a l))
      (cochainOneCoord Rc K (op W') x l)).symm) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun z => (quotientPi Rc K).val.app (op W') z)
    (mul_comm ((structureSheaf Rc).obj.map i.op (a l))
      (cochainOneCoord Rc K (op W') x l))) ?_
  exact map_smul (ConcreteCategory.hom ((quotientPi Rc K).val.app (op W')))
    (cochainOneCoord Rc K (op W') x l) _

/-- **The degree-one generator is locally surjective:** the first cohomology sheaf of
`SheafHom^•(K, K)` is generated, as a sheaf of `O♯`-modules, by the classes of the `r` coordinate
contractions.

Every local section of a cohomology sheaf is locally the class of a cocycle, and the class of a
cocycle is locally a combination of the classes of the contractions; the covering produced by the
second step is pulled back along the arrows of the first, which is the transitivity axiom of the
topology.

The local surjectivity of the homology projection is named here at the `(structureSheaf Rc).obj`
spelling of the sheaf of rings, the one `extGenerator` is indexed by: the projection itself lives
over `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf Rc`, and while that is the same sheaf of rings, the
file's `implicit_reducible` transparency is not available to instance search, so the fact has to
be in context already written at the spelling `Presheaf.imageSieve_mem` asks for. -/
instance isLocallySurjective_extGenerator [QuasiIso K.augmentation] :
    PresheafOfModules.IsLocallySurjective (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X)
      (R := (structureSheaf Rc).obj) (extGenerator Rc K).val where
  imageSieve_mem {U} t := by
    haveI hπ : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X)
        ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (structureSheaf Rc).obj).map
          ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).homologyπ 1).val) :=
      ImageSubsheaf.isLocallySurjective_of_epi ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).homologyπ 1)
    refine (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X).transitive
      (Presheaf.imageSieve_mem (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X)
        ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (structureSheaf Rc).obj).map
          ((endComplex Rc (cochain Rc K)).homologyπ 1).val) t) _ ?_
    intro V f hf
    obtain ⟨cc, hcc⟩ := hf
    rw [Presheaf.pullback_imageSieve, ← hcc]
    exact imageSieve_extGenerator_homologyπ_mem Rc K V cc

